  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Economic Justice for Women</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Socio-economic and political factors continue to negatively affect women of all ethnicities, religions and social classes preventing them from having control or influence over decisions that impact their businesses and large economic policies. This in turn leads women to be largely undervalued and unrecognised. The proposed project focuses on addressing gendered implications of the National Small to Medium Enterprise Policy in Sri Lanka through transforming structures and creating a favorable, e</narrative>
  </description>
